# ops/publish-blocklist.local — project-specific PII/secret patterns
#
# One POSIX ERE per line. Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored.
# Patterns are matched against file content with grep -rIlE (binary files skipped).
# A match on any file blocks the publish until that content is removed or
# the line is removed from this file.
#
# HOW TO USE:
#   cp ops/publish-blocklist.local.example ops/publish-blocklist.local
#   Fill in patterns for your host's real identifiers below.
#   The .local file is gitignored; only this .example is tracked.
#
# IMPORTANT: this .example file itself is exported and scanned on every
# publish — patterns in this file must NOT match themselves. Use regex
# constructs with wildcards or character classes rather than literal values.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Example: internal LAN IP ranges
# Replace [0-9]+ with the actual octets of your LAN ranges in the .local file.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 192\.168\.[0-9]+\.[0-9]+
# 10\.[0-9]+\.[0-9]+\.[0-9]+
# 172\.(1[6-9]|2[0-9]|3[01])\.[0-9]+\.[0-9]+

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Example: internal hostnames
# Replace the character class with a literal hostname prefix in the .local file.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# [a-z]+-dev[0-9]+\.internal
# devbox-[0-9]+\.lan
# [a-z]+\.corp\.example\.com

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Example: account or project ID shapes
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# [Aa]ccount[-_]?[Ii][Dd]:\s*[0-9]{8,}
# [Pp]roject[-_][Ii][Dd]=[A-Z0-9]{12,}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Example: personal path fragments
# Replace the character class with your username in the .local file.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# /home/[a-z][-a-z0-9]+/
# /Users/[A-Za-z][-A-Za-z0-9]+/projects/
